# GoShiSen-Enforce packaging Go toolchain policy (S-005 gate).
#
# This file is the single source of truth for the minimum Go toolchain
# version that EVERY shipped artifact must be built with:
#
#   - the OpenWrt apk payload (usr/sbin/goshisen)
#   - the CLI/daemon release archives (goshisen-linux-*.tar.gz)
#
# The apk payload is built by the OpenWrt SDK's golang feed (or a
# pinned toolchain injected into the SDK build), NOT by CI's Go, so
# the gates must inspect the payload's embedded buildinfo directly
# (scripts/check-apk-payload-go.sh). The release archives are built in
# release.yml with setup-go go-version == MIN_GO_VERSION and
# GOTOOLCHAIN=local.
#
# Selected 2026-11-18 after S-005 (issue #78): the published v0.2.5
# apk embedded go1.27.1 and the CLI archives go1.25.14, both carrying
# reachable stdlib vulnerabilities fixed only in go1.27.4. Go 1.27.4
# is the patch that fixes the full S-005 set (GO-2026-6859, 6809,
# 6617, 6613, 6612, 6611, 6610, 6608, 6607, 6605, 6603) — verify
# against govulncheck, never by assumption.
MIN_GO_VERSION=1.27.4
